## 5. When the docs subagent returns

- I check every snapshot claim against the evidence files and run the project's docs-only check.
- **Bash, foreground:**
  ```bash
  cd ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs && git grep -nE "code/session_[0-9A-Za-z]"   # must be empty
  git add -A && git commit -m "docs: close WireGuard keepalive relay (ccs-it snapshot, #165)"
  git push -u origin chore/wg-keepalive-docs
  gh pr create --title "docs: close WireGuard keepalive relay" --body-file $S/pr-body-T7-docs.md
  gh pr merge <n> --merge --delete-branch
  ```
- **Write** the memory file `wg-keepalive-relay-live.md` (type `project`) and its `MEMORY.md` pointer. It records the relay live on ccs-it since 2026-09-28 via #165, the evidence, the traps from my session notes, and a pointer to the snapshot.
- Backlog: `docs closed: yes`, then republish.

## 6. Cleanup, straight after

**Bash, foreground:**
```bash
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive status --porcelain   # must be empty
herdr agent get wgka                                                          # idle, focused:false
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree remove .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree remove .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive-docs
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree prune
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay chore/wg-keepalive-docs
ps -p 48211 -o pid,command && kill 48211                                      # only the broker I started
git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible pull && git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible worktree list
```
Backlog: T7 `done`, then republish and send a status.

## 7. On each advisor notification

- I read `$S/inbox/<name>.last`, then `herdr agent get <name>`, then the context usage.
- I answer `prod-fable`'s permission prompts myself: its own file only, default deny.
- I answer facts with evidence. Every choice becomes a neutral ballot, sent to `adv-codex` and `adv-fable` at once.
- Round 2 and round 3 follow, relayed by file path.

## Why

- **T7 is not done.** Acceptance is stage 12. `done` needs the docs closed and the cleanup finished. "Harmless paperwork at any time" is how the snapshot stays wrong and the broker stays running, so both run tonight alongside the brainstorm.
- **RDP audio is a new task.** It enters the backlog at `brainstorm`, and no executor may exist before the joint design is approved 2/2. The design the operator wants is the output of stage 0.
- **`wgka` is not reused.** One tab is one task, and its knowledge of the roles does not change that. Closing it is part of T7's cleanup.
- **The product advisors get their own tabs.** A voting advisor that drafted would be judging its own work.
- **I give no design hints.** The brief carries the operator's words and facts only.
- **No poll now.** A night fits three rounds, so no operator decision is pending. I do not promise the morning.
- **The status is in English** because this session's configuration requires it; the manifest's §15 asks for Russian for operator-facing text.
